  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social and Economic Justice Programmes</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programme Title: KwaZulu Natal Integrated HIV and AIDS Programme   
Programme Goal: Strengthened capacity of individuals, households and communities to respond to and mitigate the impact of HIV and AIDS in KZN.
Project goal: Mobilised local churches for active engagement in socio-economic transformation within the eThekwini municipal area.  
Outcomes:
1. Increased mainstreaming of gender, human rights, HIV and AIDS in social justice issues.
2. Increased participation of local churches in democracy, governance issues and public participation processes.
3. Women involved in Self Help Groups (SHGs) have the capacity to claim their socio-economic rights
4. Local churches empowered for healing and reconciliation to engage in social justice issues.
5. Local churches actively engaged in meaningful economic transformation within the eThekwini municipal area.
6. Local churches take ownership of the Social Justice Season through active mobilisation of other local churches.

Through the implementation of the Social and Economic Justice Programme, Diakonia together with communities, individuals and families in KwaZulu Natal, South Africa intend to mobilise local churches for active engagement in socio-economic transformation. This programme will focus its energies within the eThekwini municipal area targeting the poor, marginalized women and children and excluded members of the communities. Uniquely, the programme will use Facilitation, accompaniment, capacity building, advocacy and lobbying, service access, research, information dissemination, awareness raising, networking and partnership as the preferred methods of programme implementation. Further, pillars to this response will be mainstreaming HIV and AIDS, Gender and Human Rights. This project will feed into a broader 3 year programme - KwaZulu Natal Integrated Development Programme being implemented by 5 other partners.</narrative>
  </description>
